  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1030 PM MDT Sat Oct 10 2026\n\nThe remnants of Rachel have merged/been absorbed into a larger\ntrough, aligned along the West Coast. Well out ahead of the\ntrough, moisture is being drawn northward with some hints of\ndiffluence aloft over NM, Chihuahua, and Far West TX. The result \nis isolated showers, which have weakened some with the loss of \ndaytime heating. The 00z EPZ sounding showed shallow CAPE with \nmost of it rooted below the dendrite/ice growth zone (-10 deg C), \nso lightning was non-existent though a few cells still had some\ndecent cores on radar. Shower coverage should continue to \ndecrease through the rest of the night although chances will be \nnon-zero.\n\nThe UL low will lift northeast with the right-entrance region of\nthe jet moving over NM on Sunday. With continued moisture, this\nwill lead to additional showers and storms, favoring areas along\nand east of the Rio Grande. The HRRR is on board with this\nscenario. Although the trough remains anchored to our west on\nMonday, favorable jet dynamics will wane with rain chances\nshifting toward AZ, possibly the Gila. \n\nUL trough will still be anchored to our west on Tuesday, but\nremnant moisture from Hurricane Simon will be pulled far enough\nnorth to enter Texas. Chances of any precip for our CWA continue\nto dwindle, but a shower or thunderstorm from Simon could still\nclip parts of Hudspeth County. \n\nThe UL low will finally begin to lift out by Wednesday and\nThursday with dry air completely moving into the CWA. As the low\nenters the Plains, it will force a cold front southward, pushing\nthrough the CWA late Thursday night, early Friday morning. Friday\nwill be noticeably cooler. In terms of precip chances, both the \nGFS and Euro lag a piece of the trough behind, likely in response \nto the cold front, but the GFS reforms a closed low well to our \nSW, keeping us dry. The Euro keeps more of the trough back, \nclosing it off of the Colorado River Valley, but that puts us in \nfavorable moisture advection. A look at the LREF shows the Euro \nand GFS ensembles are both favoring their deterministic \ncounterpart. NBM has some low to moderate POPs, which seems \nreasonable enough.",
